# The callee reads the pair and keeps no reference to it, so the pair lies in the frame of the caller: the likely path calls no allocator, and the stores need neither a barrier nor a fence.
# Its state byte says that it is no cell of the heap. Both references are stored in front of the call, so whoever walks the frame during the call finds them.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="pick" role=Source
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint(
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[pair]] = SlotBase(stack0, {{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint(
# CHECK-NOT: Fence(
# CHECK: Store8($255(b@{{*}}), b@[[pair]], offset = 7, ControlDependent|Writes:collectorState, {{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint(
# CHECK-NOT: Fence(
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:collectorState
# CHECK: Store(b@[[left]], b@[[pair]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint(
# CHECK-NOT: Fence(
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:collectorState
# CHECK: Store(b@[[right]], b@[[pair]], offset = 24, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[heavier]] = Patchpoint(b@[[pair]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), {{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: Return(b@[[heavier]], Terminal)
# CHECK: Stack slots:
# CHECK-NEXT: stack0: byteSize = 32, 
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
